  "meta": {
    "name": "09 · Memory (Write → Read)",
    "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t09_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Memory across frames: Write → Read\n\nThe patch runs once a frame, left to right. To keep a value from one frame to the next, end the flow with a Write and start it with its Read. The two are a pair (named \"counter\" here); no wire runs back.\n• The Read at the left gives the value the Write stored last frame (on the very first frame, its `init`).\n• Whatever reaches the Write's `next` is what the Read gives on the next frame.\n\nHere the count goes through +1 into the Write, so it grows by 1 every frame and turns the hue.",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 260
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Memory across frames: Write → Read\n\nThe patch runs once a frame, left to right. To keep a value from one frame to the next, end the flow with a Write and start it with its Read. The two are a pair (named \"counter\" here); no wire runs back.\n• The Read at the left gives the value the Write stored last frame (on the very first frame, its `init`).\n• Whatever reaches the Write's `next` is what the Read gives on the next frame.\n\nHere the count goes through +1 into the Write, so it grows by 1 every frame and turns the hue.",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
